{"name":"Homoeopathic Lavender","hex":"#e5e0ec","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"homoeopathic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative spelling of homeopathic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/homoeopathic"},{"term":"lavender","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of a group of European plants, genus, Lavandula, of the mint family.","A pale bluish purple or violet colour, like that of the lavender flower."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a pale purple colour.","Pertaining to LGBT people and rights."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lavender"}],"entries":[{"title":"Homeopathy","blocks":[{"text":"Homeopathy or homoeopathy is a pseudoscientific system of alternative medicine. It was conceived in 1796 by the German physician Samuel Hahnemann. Its practitioners, called homeopaths or homeopathic physicians, believe that a substance that causes symptoms of a disease in healthy people can cure similar symptoms in sick people; this doctrine is called similia similibus curentur, or \"like cures like\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Saxonia_Museum_fuer_saechsische_Vaterlandskunde_III_19.jpg/330px-Saxonia_Museum_fuer_saechsische_Vaterlandskunde_III_19.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homeopathy","wikidata":"Q81058"},{"title":"Lavandula","blocks":[{"text":"Lavandula is a genus of 47 known species of perennial flowering plants in the sage family, Lamiaceae. It is native to regions of the Iberian Peninsula and Mediterranean coastline, the Middle East, extending to the Indian subcontinent."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Single_lavender_flower02.jpg/330px-Single_lavender_flower02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lavandula","wikidata":"Q171892"},{"title":"Lavender (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lavender is a light shade of purple or violet. It applies particularly to the color of the flower of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Lavandula_fields.jpg/330px-Lavandula_fields.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lavender_(color)","wikidata":"Q2468392"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Homeopathy-2.jpg/500px-Homeopathy-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Homeopathy-2.jpg/1280px-Homeopathy-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Homeopathy-2.jpg/500px-Homeopathy-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHomeopathy-2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Samuel_Hahnemann_Monument%2C_Scott_Circle.jpg/500px-Samuel_Hahnemann_Monument%2C_Scott_Circle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Samuel_Hahnemann_Monument%2C_Scott_Circle.jpg/1280px-Samuel_Hahnemann_Monument%2C_Scott_Circle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Samuel_Hahnemann_Monument%2C_Scott_Circle.jpg/500px-Samuel_Hahnemann_Monument%2C_Scott_Circle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Samuel Hahnemann Monument, Washington, D.C., with the inscription Similia Similibus Curentur – \"Like cures Like\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASamuel_Hahnemann_Monument%2C_Scott_Circle.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedi